From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:23:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Monotone::Monotone: fill mNotesHz from entry 1

The table below note 1 was filled down to entry 2, leaving entry 1
uninitialised; vibrato on note 1 reads it. The loop now runs down to
entry 1, continuing the table.
---
 src/audiosource/monotone/soloud_monotone.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/monotone/soloud_monotone.cpp b/src/audiosource/monotone/soloud_monotone.cpp
index 3791c13..e31ffda 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/monotone/soloud_monotone.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/monotone/soloud_monotone.cpp
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@ namespace SoLoud
 		mNotesHz[0] = 440;
 		mNotesHz[1 * IBN] = (int)floor(temphz + 0.5f);
 
-		for (i = (1 * IBN) - 1; i > 1; i--)
+		for (i = (1 * IBN) - 1; i > 0; i--)
 		{
 			temphz = temphz / interval;
 			if (temphz < 19) temphz = 19; // orig limitation, we could go lower though
